# Obsidian setup

Open **`kb/`** as the vault, not the repository root. OKF links such as
`/systems/dns.md` are bundle-root paths, and Obsidian resolves a leading `/`
against the vault root. The two only agree when they are the same folder.

## Already configured (committed in `kb/.obsidian/`)

| Setting | Value | Why |
|---|---|---|
| Use [[Wikilinks]] | off | OKF links are standard markdown links. Typing `[[` still autocompletes, but inserts a markdown link. |
| New link format | Path from vault folder | Better Markdown Links (below) adds the leading `/`. `just fix` repairs any link written without it. |
| Automatically update internal links | on | Renames inside Obsidian keep links working. `just fix` restores the `/` form afterwards. |
| Deleted files | Move to system trash | A `.trash/` folder inside the vault would add non-conformant `.md` files to the bundle. |
| Properties in document | Source | The Properties UI re-serializes the whole YAML block, reordering keys and dropping quotes, which makes noisy diffs. Edit frontmatter as text. |
| Default location for new notes | Same folder as current file | |
| Attachment folder | `assets` | |
| Daily notes | `journal/YYYY/YYYY-MM-DD`, template `_templates/journal-entry` | |
| Graph filter | `-file:index.md -file:log.md -path:_templates` | Without it, generated indexes become hubs that distort the graph. |
| Core plugins | Bases, Daily notes, Backlinks, Outgoing links, Outline, Page preview, Properties, Bookmarks, Footnotes view… | Core Templates is off; Templater replaces it. |

## Install these community plugins

Go to *Settings → Community plugins → Browse*. The vault lists them as
enabled, but Obsidian only loads them once installed.

| Plugin | Configure | Role |
|---|---|---|
| **Templater** | Already configured: templates folder `_templates`, folder template for `journal/`. Turn **"Trigger Templater on new file creation"** on yourself, because it is a per-device setting. | Templates set a valid OKF frontmatter on new notes. |
| **Better Markdown Links** | Make sure "Use leading slash for absolute paths" is on (the default). | Writes `/…` links. |
| **Front Matter Title** | Enable it for the explorer, tabs, graph and search, with the title key `title`. | Shows titles instead of filenames, which matters because many files are called `index`. |
| **Folder notes** | Folder note name: `index`. Don't let it create folder notes automatically: `index.md` files are generated. | Clicking a folder opens its index. |
| **Breadcrumbs** | Add one edge field per relation key in `schema/vocabulary.yaml` (`part_of` as "up"). | Navigates the typed relations stored as markdown links in frontmatter. |
| **Linter** | YAML key sort, priority order: `type, title, description, aliases, resource, author, published, archived, tags, status, generated, verified, stale_after, sources`, then the relation keys. Leave "lint on save" **off** for `_templates/`. | Keeps frontmatter tidy. It cannot validate. `kb check` does that. |
| **Omnisearch** | Defaults. | Better full-text search in the app. |

**Optional:** OKF Enforcer (on-save OKF validation, still young), Excalidraw,
and Tasks.

**Avoid:**

- **Wikilink Types**, **Dataview link fields**, **ExcaliBrain**, **Juggl**
  and **Graph Link Types**: they only understand `[[wikilinks]]`.
- **Periodic Notes**: unmaintained.
- **Obsidian Git**: commits happen from the CLI or the agent.

## Dashboards

`_views/` holds Bases files, which are YAML rather than `.md`, so they sit
outside OKF:

- `knowledge.base`: every knowledge page by type, plus recent changes;
- `review-queue.base`: unverified pages, drafts and stale pages; add
  `verified` after you review a page;
- `sources.base`: ingested sources.

## Writing by hand

- **Journal:** open today's daily note.
- **Other pages:** use *Templater: Create new note from template*, choosing
  `knowledge-page` or `decision-record`.
- **Links:** use `[[` autocomplete, which writes markdown links, or link
  directly with `[Title](/folder/page.md)`.
- Run `just fix` and `just check` before committing. The pre-commit hook
  runs both.
